      "side": 1,
      "message": "As discussed, we probably want to @SuppressLint ExecutorRegistration for this method, for consistency with all the other NetworkCallback methods. This not just because the API surface will be inconsistent, it\u0027s because until all of them have overloads that take Executor, apps will have to use both Executor and Handler, and that is going to be racy. Plus, the Executor overloads will not be available on older OS releases, so...\n\nMaybe add a TODO to add Executor overloads for all these methods? Any method that passed in an Executor could process the messages on the singleton ConnectivityThread Handler.\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\n\nPlease fix this ERROR reported by Build Warnings: Registration methods should have overload that accepts delivery Executor: `reserveNetwork` (ErrorWhenNew) [ExecutorRegistration]\n\nAnalyzer Description: Reports warnings that originate from build.log in the build artifacts.\nOwner: farivar@google.com\n\n    Registration methods should have overload that accepts delivery Executor: `reserveNetwork` (ErrorWhenNew) [ExecutorRegistration]\n\nThis finding was found on https://android-build.googleplex.com/builds/build-details/P87385596/targets/cf_x86_64_phone-trunk_staging-userdebug, but may also be present on other builds.\n\nThis is a different branch than your cl originated on (it was automerged), and thus might better reflect the state of the code in the git_main branch.",
